# Mode Study: A Mixolydian (repertoire plan: st-mode-mixolydian). An original 16-bar melody over a
# two-chord vamp: A (x02220) for two bars, then G (320003) for two. G natural, the flat seventh,
# is the colour of Mixolydian: a major scale with a bluesy, folk-rock edge.
# The melody lands on G on a strong beat in bars 3, 4, 7, 11, 12 and 15, over the G chord, and
# passes through it over A in bars 2, 5, 10 and 13. The last bars change faster (G in bar 15,
# A in bar 16), so the tune ends G to A: the flat seventh rising home.
# Second position with open strings: finger 1 on fret 2, finger 2 on fret 3 (G on string 1),
# finger 4 on fret 5; open E and G ring in the line.
title: Mode Study: A Mixolydian
